# armour/man/leather: boiled / studded leather on the man (P2c slice, SLICE-ARMOUR; re-shaded by LADDER-ARMOUR for value,
# STYLE_P2 25.2, 27.5 C14): matte and warm, light (the civilian silhouette kept). The owner: the archer was "brown on
# brown", so the values now part: a broad lit plane at the top-left (step 3) with one step-4 shine on the lit shoulder, a
# step-1 shadow side, ONE step-1 seam across the chest, a DARK belt band (step 1) at the waist with its buckle, and a
# SOLID LIT HEM (step 3 into 2) so the jerkin parts from dark trousers below it and the cloth at the collar above it.
# The studs (T2, the `studs` ornament) are the `when studs` region: one course of metal-2 pixels on the lit chest.
# Finish regions (contracts 3b): R the hem, P the chest's lit plane, G a stud socket on the chest, N the seam, W a 2x2
# spot (a patch at T1) on the shadow side. Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L.
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's expand.py.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i1, P3) the fitted jerkin: a yoke seam across the chest (step 1), a chest strap with its
# buckle (metal 2) above the belt, a solid lit plane on the left: T2 reads as cut and fitted, not a brown sack.
use person
body man
role armour leather
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2

